er/id #uuid "9ebdad6a-41c8-59ad-af2d-d72af1deabc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473607} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca8bfa6b-b929-5e74-80aa-3b5b316eeba5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474198} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f89864d9-d767-5f8d-ba22-642be7cf1213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473608} {:answer/id #uuid "123eea51-48b5-53a9-b7ce-0110b86f53ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "123eea51-48b5-53a9-b7ce-0110b86f53ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473609} :answer-field/id #uuid "43158257-ec4b-5929-bea8-451716d8f491" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6641b4f-e396-5ff5-8410-bd9f53c4e8d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-98339" :question/problem "![](images/98/9836234d763ccb3da6b9ac0360dcb3662cacc5fc90d5ecc2dee20bf29ce0c77d.png)\n\nWhich of the curves above is simple, closed, and negatively oriented?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A simple closed curve is positively oriented if, when traveling along it, one always has the curve interior to the left and the curve exterior to the right. Otherwise, the curve is negatively oriented. \n\nA curve is positively oriented if it is traversed counterclockwise and is negatively oriented if it is traversed clockwise.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the curves:\n\n- Curve I is neither simple nor closed.\n\n- Curve II is a simple and closed curve but it is not negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed counterclockwise, so it is positively oriented.\n\n- Curve III is simple, closed, negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\n- Curve IV is simple, closed, negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "630cd12d-1141-51ae-8f2e-a881622868e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Transitive Relations in Special Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f66032c-e554-543d-8fb7-d02dece4fb60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472988} {:answer/id #uuid "503722a1-9d9c-52aa-81fc-6a411eae1066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "503722a1-9d9c-52aa-81fc-6a411eae1066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472989} :answer-field/id #uuid "ded48b57-0e55-5867-8ce5-09520070f5ca" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473889} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf4b3082-da87-5935-8a6d-c02d7c283455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472990} {:answer/id #uuid "60bece86-b150-57aa-9c00-90ecd30c70e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60bece86-b150-57aa-9c00-90ecd30c70e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472991} :answer-field/id #uuid "755bfb35-b9d2-5062-b4ab-e488a159dfa7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "279c4aba-6d55-5a04-b286-e063ea4fc0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472992} {:answer/id #uuid "733b09d3-0ca0-56fd-b468-a6f12122fc9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "733b09d3-0ca0-56fd-b468-a6f12122fc9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472993} :answer-field/id #uuid "242b2c29-1e00-59da-9422-d72051cd8ab7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473891} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbf5caaf-107c-5cf9-9a1b-17712be4c02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472994} {:answer/id #uuid "bf886d4c-aafd-5159-a9c1-995083aabdef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf886d4c-aafd-5159-a9c1-995083aabdef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472995} :answer-field/id #uuid "18afe69d-87a8-5ebb-b3e6-8e65d1302ff0" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "202c6abf-dfb5-522a-9256-456835ce12bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-214430" :question/problem "Which of the following relations on the set $A={1,3,5,7}$ are transitive?\n- **I.** ${R}_{1}=∅$\n- **II.** ${R}_{2}={A}^{2}$\n- **III.** ${R}_{3}={(5,5)}$\n- **IV.** ${R}_{4}={(5,1),(7,3)}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R$ defined on a set $A$ is *transitive* if, for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,z)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(x,z)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if the pairs $(x,y)$ and $(y,z)$ belong to a transitive relation, then the pair $(x,z)$ should also be in the relation.\n\nIt's sufficient to check all the \"linked\" pairs of the form $(x,y)$ with $x\\ne y$ and $(y,z)$ with $y\\ne z:$\n\nMoreover, we recall the following:\n\n- The universal relation $R={A}^{2}$ is transitive since it includes all possible ordered pairs.\n\n- The empty relation $R=∅$ is vacuously transitive since the antecedent in the implication is always false, and therefore the implication is always true.\n\n- A relation containing no \"linked\" pairs is always transitive.\n\n- A relation containing only reflexive pairs is always transitive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations:\n\n- ${R}_{1}$ is transitive since it's the empty relation. $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${R}_{2}$ is transitive since it's the universal relation. $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${R}_{3}$ is transitive since it contains only reflexive pairs.  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${R}_{4}$ is transitive since it contains no \"linked\" pairs.  $\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418244 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "630cd12d-1141-51ae-8f2e-a881622868e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Transitive Relations in Special Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a299c676-d4bd-5e7c-9a2c-0554e7b11068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472996} {:answer/id #uuid "94f3ebe8-49c9-50b3-a868-e5d33ab917ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94f3ebe8-49c9-50b3-a868-e5d33ab917ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472997} :answer-field/id #uuid "174d226d-d258-5803-bd1a-f8c8044e8e61" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e37eca59-a651-5ae5-a63a-f7c00a6e9ee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472998} {:answer/id #uuid "d58460b0-5da4-55d1-9273-6866444c5ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d58460b0-5da4-55d1-9273-6866444c5ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472999} :answer-field/id #uuid "64720d48-f6ec-5b01-9b7a-d890a7e21109" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2625fa0-6fd0-5b37-8bcb-85e89aaf9f1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473000} {:answer/id #uuid "6549efa0-c3e5-513f-a9c4-a86cc73d7989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6549efa0-c3e5-513f-a9c4-a86cc73d7989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473001} :answer-field/id #uuid "1908c829-a51f-5ba0-bef7-0ed5edbdf979" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473895} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ead24d32-9ef3-517d-bc6c-fa5541e27250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473002} {:answer/id #uuid "9afd106d-a0c9-585d-8d8b-f5c66a4f5e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9afd106d-a0c9-585d-8d8b-f5c66a4f5e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473003} :answer-field/id #uuid "586bc858-e57d-5502-9bc1-05c0b7811913" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "44cd3428-3b1c-5e19-9525-5e86c3ca616a" :question/math-academy-id "q-214431" :question/problem "Which of the following relations on the set $A={♢,♡,♠,♣}$ are transitive?\n- **I.** ${R}_{1}={(♢,♢),(♣,♣)}$\n- **II.** ${R}_{2}={(♠,♠)}$\n- **III.** ${R}_{3}={(♢,♠),(♡,♣)}$\n- **IV.** ${R}_{4}=∅$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R$ defined on a set $A$ is *transitive* if, for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,z)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(x,z)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if the pairs $(x,y)$ and $(y,z)$ belong to a transitive relation, then the pair $(x,z)$ should also be in the relation.\n\nIt's sufficient to check all the \"linked\" pairs of the form $(x,y)$ with $x\\ne y$ and $(y,z)$ with $y\\ne z:$\n\nMoreover, we recall the following:\n\n- The universal relation $R={A}^{2}$ is transitive since it includes all possible ordered pairs.\n\n- The empty relation $R=∅$ is vacuously transitive since the antecedent in the implication is always false, and therefore the implication is always true.\n\n- A relation containing no \"linked\" pairs is always transitive.\n\n- A relation containing only reflexive pairs is always transitive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations:\n\n- ${R}_{1}$ is transitive since it contains only reflexive pairs.  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${R}_{2}$ is transitive since it contains only reflexive pairs.  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${R}_{3}$ is transitive since it contains no \"linked\" pairs.  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${R}_{4}$ is transitive since it's the empty relation. $\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418246 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203887 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f65dc026-1ec7-51f3-abc2-4a8ce95f9c2c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Transitive Relations From a Digraph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4db8a7d3-abfe-5da7-8f35-9f33f9974fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472982} {:answer/id #uuid "bee0ee00-25f3-5d6b-ab69-c0475d9b0cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4db8a7d3-abfe-5da7-8f35-9f33f9974fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472982} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4178680-7a42-51f7-b05b-b18ebe268db9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473886} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "820a5684-a957-5349-a0f0-7963f49ebe66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472984} {:answer/id #uuid "93478089-576c-5503-80b8-3e9d093c765c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93478089-576c-5503-80b8-3e9d093c765c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472985} :answer-field/id #uuid "b558f1b5-b2d4-5cbe-8db1-9b06242983c2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e021bd35-f594-5b3a-b63d-34b162014252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472986} {:answer/id #uuid "e516049f-9d3f-5de6-aacd-690ed76c7a97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e021bd35-f594-5b3a-b63d-34b162014252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472986} :answer-field/id #uuid "739e0d22-4e64-5fd6-9771-aa129ae1e27d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64ea6724-f6be-5851-a399-860e0e1924d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-214065" :question/problem "![](images/1f/1fa323b54736f62bb334ae491d8d41deeba4a4e325f6e56f9651da147d50c349.png)\n\nWhich of the above digraphs represents a transitive relation defined on the set $A={p,q,r}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R$ defined on a set $A$ is *transitive* if, for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,z)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(x,z)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if the pairs $(x,y)$ and $(y,z)$ belong to a transitive relation, then the pair $(x,z)$ should also be in the relation.\n\nIt's sufficient to check all the \"linked\" pairs of the form $(x,y)$ with $x\\ne y$ and $(y,z)$ with $y\\ne z.$\n\nIn terms of a digraph, if we have \"linked\" arrows $x\\to y$ and $y\\to z,$ then the arrow $x\\to z$ must be in the digraph too.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our digraphs.\n\n- Digraph I does not represent a transitive relation. It has arrows $q\\to r$ and $r\\to p,$ but has no arrow $q\\to p.$\n\n- Digraph II represents a transitive relation. For any pair of arrows $x\\to y$ and $y\\to z,$ the arrow  $x\\to z$ also belongs to the digraph.\n\n- Digraph III does not represent a transitive relation. It has arrows $p\\to q$ and $q\\to r,$ but has no arrow $p\\to r.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "947f058c-4c47-52df-8c28-aed016d2b148" :knowledge-point/title "Transitive Relations Defined On Infinite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4570740-e38d-5619-a596-b27434de2acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472976} {:answer/id #uuid "2445e097-f060-51a2-9b4f-786c2564057b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2445e097-f060-51a2-9b4f-786c2564057b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472977} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2928ca7-454a-561d-a28f-37c83fce06c0" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473883} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a72744f6-7c6e-5b96-8a5c-21c64adc05c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472978} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8c1316-7031-5bf4-b390-e30b6262259d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a72744f6-7c6e-5b96-8a5c-21c64adc05c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472978} :answer-field/id #uuid "540b176a-d122-565a-8e22-9c2f73677d72" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0db7216-4608-5567-9227-6f5edb180769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472980} {:answer/id #uuid "808ff085-7391-520c-bb65-0806364a6656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "808ff085-7391-520c-bb65-0806364a6656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472981} :answer-field/id #uuid "7315c86a-eebd-57ce-ac6f-9eaaeeb953b9" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "70eb9024-0964-59ad-a103-f6948d25a78c" :question/math-academy-id "q-214002" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are transitive?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **R.** $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∣y,$ defined on $Z$\n\n- **S.** $x\\,S\\,y$ if and only if $x+y<4,$ defined on $R$\n\n- **T.** $x\\,T\\,y$ if and only if $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4),$ defined on $Z$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R$ defined on a set $A$ is *transitive* if, for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,z)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(x,z)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if the pairs $(x,y)$ and $(y,z)$ belong to a transitive relation, then the pair $(x,z)$ should also be in the relation.\n\nIt's sufficient to check all the \"linked\" pairs of the form $(x,y)$ with $x\\ne y$ and $(y,z)$ with $y\\ne z.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is transitive. Indeed, if $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,x)\\in R,$ then $(x,z)\\in R.$ Notice that \n\n$$\nx∣y\\,\\text{and}\\,y∣z\\,⟹\\,x∣z\n$$\n\nfor all $x,y,z\\in Z.$\n\n- Relation $S$ is not transitive. Notice that \n\n- $(1,-4)\\in S$ since $1+(-4)=-3<4,$ and\n\n- $(-4,5)\\in S$ since $-4+5=1<4,$ but\n\n- $(1,5)\\notin S$ since $1+5=6≮4.$\n\n- Relation $T$ is transitive. Indeed, if $(x,y)\\in T$ and $(y,x)\\in T,$ then $(x,z)\\in T.$ Notice that \n\n$$\nx≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\\,\\text{and}\\,y≡z\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\\,⟹\\,x≡z\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\n$$\n\nfor all $x,y,z\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$R$ and $T$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f0a57c2-bbad-5225-976b-385c7f117738" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Poisson Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fafa6def-aaf0-5ba2-855c-6a88e1f98666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473476} {:answer/id #uuid "9cffd3ba-fa84-5eda-ba42-26c885538925" :answer/type {:db/id #