 :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473474} {:answer/id #uuid "c860712b-ae9c-5579-ad3d-c1e0cac398f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e119bd7-8ecb-5809-93c3-32cd6e210a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473474} :answer-field/id #uuid "c42974fb-206f-53e3-b05f-8bf8666ca76c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d411b05d-363a-5c38-b187-cabf795e2dff" :question/math-academy-id "q-85316" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled using a Poisson distribution?\n- **I.** The number of visits a web page has per minute\n- **II.** The number of works of art created by a sculptor in a period of one year\n- **III.** The average height of the players on a basketball team\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A Poisson distribution models the number of events that occur in an interval of time or space if events occur independently and at a constant average rate.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I follows a Poisson distribution. The number of visits on a web page can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a minute).\n\n- Random variable II follows a Poisson distribution. The number of works of art can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a year).\n\n- Random variable III does *not* follow a Poisson distribution. There are no events that occur at a constant average rate, and there is no interval of time or space.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04e719c2-0320-5791-b983-6b439ef537de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472856} {:answer/id #uuid "6c0b13a1-62f1-5553-bcbd-448f6af6e81a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c0b13a1-62f1-5553-bcbd-448f6af6e81a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472857} :answer-field/id #uuid "7659e378-9a5a-5e51-9c6b-123e8db92f8c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cc110b0-980a-5da9-a368-1d441f2e14e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472858} {:answer/id #uuid "23cabb60-197b-58d3-b057-a401c9b60c3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23cabb60-197b-58d3-b057-a401c9b60c3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472859} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff5bb257-fc6a-5969-bd76-b2f265fb880a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e7fcce6-9840-5474-ac13-57b36e28e608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472860} {:answer/id #uuid "802680a9-a6a4-5def-9609-d2a7a40f477f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e7fcce6-9840-5474-ac13-57b36e28e608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472860} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ecee75d-11c5-5fba-8893-0cddff0394f7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "237ee44c-ddeb-50a9-b28f-87d4edfa4e60" :question/math-academy-id "q-212521" :question/problem "Given that $-21≡-12\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=3$\n- **II.** $n=9$\n- **III.** $n=12$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=-21-(-12)=-9.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $3∣(-9)$ because $(-9)÷3=-3,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=3.$\n\n- Note that $9∣(-9)$ because $(-9)÷9=-1,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=9.$\n\n- Note that $12∤(-9).$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=12.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b22152ce-58df-5d5c-a9a7-ba02352c55aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473338} {:answer/id #uuid "076c6326-e56f-5a55-8cce-576ee8ff3ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "076c6326-e56f-5a55-8cce-576ee8ff3ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473339} :answer-field/id #uuid "53684faa-202a-5928-b132-14a5034a255a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474064} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80af74f8-1f7d-51ed-b670-9aaae0e5d2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473340} {:answer/id #uuid "25113294-a512-5863-9023-b0167b7c809f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80af74f8-1f7d-51ed-b670-9aaae0e5d2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473340} :answer-field/id #uuid "3777b970-73d5-5c49-89c5-8d64d21f5000" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474065} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9163e2b9-954f-5fd6-b2fe-291b223e344c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473342} {:answer/id #uuid "8e501603-638e-55de-adf9-ab132ae2ca0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e501603-638e-55de-adf9-ab132ae2ca0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473343} :answer-field/id #uuid "d013da85-465d-5629-92e9-fa4b42ff4a9a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7dad68af-5609-5774-82ac-907f4e4304f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-76962" :question/problem "Given that $19≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=7$\n- **II.** $n=9$\n- **III.** $n=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=19-5=14.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $7∣14$ because $14÷7=2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=7.$\n\n- Note that $9∤14.$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=9.$\n\n- Note that $2∣14$ because $14÷2=7,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29c4d9e7-fcc1-51cb-9feb-d14eed398feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472754} {:answer/id #uuid "48e4a354-249b-5ba2-9117-b2967ef925f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48e4a354-249b-5ba2-9117-b2967ef925f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472755} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd5de993-b98b-510c-aca5-b262d4fe57ab" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2776862c-c124-5cdd-a3a8-95305ed05171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472756} {:answer/id #uuid "ff8c4bf0-30a7-5205-a922-7ff4168cd4ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2776862c-c124-5cdd-a3a8-95305ed05171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472756} :answer-field/id #uuid "7496452b-de20-5cb6-96eb-ad9d02d388c8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473773} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b9e0b92-1b40-59a0-a102-0725a2933668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472758} {:answer/id #uuid "685a4b07-2685-5bcc-833d-6284d65a3096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "685a4b07-2685-5bcc-833d-6284d65a3096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472759} :answer-field/id #uuid "869b058e-5f7d-52b3-ba22-dde49434dad4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "08bf8696-2d24-58a9-b5b4-856286859054" :question/math-academy-id "q-160646" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at  $(-1,3),(-2,2),(1,-4).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n- **I.** $(3,1)$\n- **II.** $(2,-2)$\n- **III.** $(-4,-1)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ is the same as counterclockwise rotation by an angle of ${270}^{∘}.$ It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(3,1),(2,2),(-4,-1).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420276 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ad9700-5aaa-5b00-8d2f-acce6ed59c9a" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "982f653f-6cf3-53fc-8e56-92ef7d70036a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473016} {:answer/id #uuid "edcc72a5-120b-5ee1-97e7-fd2c98eb5894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edcc72a5-120b-5ee1-97e7-fd2c98eb5894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473017} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaa6136d-b30b-56e8-bf30-53b61fc6705c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473903} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7ee2327-d1e9-55df-aa68-0c11381e1802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473018} {:answer/id #uuid "2feb2a73-5b5f-5e62-a646-b09fcd1fd29a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2feb2a73-5b5f-5e62-a646-b09fcd1fd29a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473019} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddb77040-d533-5459-9ba9-3ae4efed3106" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473904} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4606e02b-20d0-5cfc-93eb-144ed9f379b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473020} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb21794-a922-514c-b6d9-2a4e071ad20c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeb21794-a922-514c-b6d9-2a4e071ad20c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473021} :answer-field/id #uuid "d26a451b-cb27-5bb6-a13a-9b40b67b59dd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba992cb2-fd2f-5e4c-b95b-b82e7bb29b58" :question/math-academy-id "q-232536" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)={3}^{x}+1?$\n\nI. The range of $f$ is $(1,\\infty )$\n\nII. $∀\\,y\\in (1,\\infty ),$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\nIII. $f$ maps $R$ **into** $R$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/0c/0cb3e23cecdbd82803f5757827f21a424672bdde6da03782ca995d23e1c4d7b4.png)\n\nRecall that $f:X\\to Y$ is an *into* function if it is not a surjection. In other words, there exists an element $y$ in $Y$ such that it has no preimage in $X:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an into function if $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, the function takes all $y$-values greater than $y=1$, excluding $y=1$ itself. So the range of the function is indeed $(1,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since the range of the function is $(1,\\infty )$, then for all $y$ contained within $(1,\\infty ),$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x$ such that $f(x)=0\\in R.$ So, $f$ maps $R$ *into* $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420329 