lue "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472806} {:answer/id #uuid "3993f4fd-fbdd-548c-b5de-850da57be767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3993f4fd-fbdd-548c-b5de-850da57be767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472807} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b7e5322-7530-5e96-9303-0361ea826df6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "787ecee8-f1f0-5525-9f42-a25a7295c8af" :question/math-academy-id "q-181669" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A={n\\in Z\\,:\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2n\\pi )=0}$\n\n- **II.** $B={q\\in Q\\,:\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2q\\pi )=0}$\n\n- **III.** $C={x\\in R\\,:\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x\\pi )=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\nWe start by finding the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x\\pi )=0$ for $x\\in R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\pi  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+m\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{m}{2},\\,m\\in Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets:\n\n- The set $A$ is finite. There are no values of $m\\in Z$ such that $\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{m}{2}\\in Z.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nA={}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|A|=0,$ which is finite.\n\n- The set $B$ is infinite. Listing the elements of $B$ for different values of $m,$ we have\n\n$$\nB={…,-\\frac{3}{4},-\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{3}{4},…}.\n$$\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Since $B$ is infinite, and $B⊆C,$ it follows that $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ and $C$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198271 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26758016-ed47-562a-9338-85c71ffbeaa9" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eeb0bd26-a87f-5160-86c6-c88af654a1c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472790} {:answer/id #uuid "058a62c1-4870-5eee-97d2-27a48de6c20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "058a62c1-4870-5eee-97d2-27a48de6c20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472791} :answer-field/id #uuid "76792b10-9c83-5ec3-991b-6d887a31bad1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473790} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b31da9e-5fdc-54f8-b67b-d7fd5360d29b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472792} {:answer/id #uuid "5883f247-a0a6-5d1a-8e80-822a5710f87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b31da9e-5fdc-54f8-b67b-d7fd5360d29b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472792} :answer-field/id #uuid "79e111f3-86c2-566b-93bc-79837883bf7b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473791} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97702641-8974-5fba-ba14-8a27155d2a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472794} {:answer/id #uuid "7e961b21-e701-5dc8-b49d-89b3c52beb1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97702641-8974-5fba-ba14-8a27155d2a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472794} :answer-field/id #uuid "63997d18-6e6c-51b4-907b-4e51f65b898a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6b24cf2-2976-579e-8d0e-dd268f3c65a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-181641" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A={{f}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}({e}^{1-2x})\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$\n\n- **II.** $B={{g}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(3{e}^{x})\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$\n\n- **III.** $C={{h}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(4{e}^{-x})\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{(0)}(x) & ={e}^{1-2x} \\\\ {f}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{1-2x})=-2{e}^{1-2x} \\\\ {f}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{e}^{1-2x})=4{e}^{1-2x} \\\\ {f}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{1-2x})=-8{e}^{1-2x} \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nA={{e}^{1-2x},-2{e}^{1-2x},4{e}^{1-2x},-8{e}^{1-2x},…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $A$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $B$ is finite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{(0)}(x) & =3{e}^{x} \\\\ {g}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{e}^{x})=3{e}^{x} \\\\ {g}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{e}^{x})=3{e}^{x} \\\\ {g}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{e}^{x})=3{e}^{x} \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $B$ contains only one element:\n\n$$\nB={3{e}^{x}}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|B|=1,$ which is finite.\n\n- The set $C$ is finite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{(0)}(x) & =4{e}^{-x} \\\\ {h}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{-x})=-4{e}^{-x} \\\\ {h}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4{e}^{-x})=4{e}^{-x} \\\\ {h}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{-x})=-4{e}^{-x} \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $C$ contains only two elements:\n\n$$\nC={4{e}^{-x},-4{e}^{-x}}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|C|=2,$ which is finite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198270 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f98332fd-e902-5390-a4d3-4e181ce97219" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Trigonometric Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6be98ed-2985-5a4b-9efa-6c626ef083aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472796} {:answer/id #uuid "a284a952-4302-5dfa-bf25-723f91b9dfd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a284a952-4302-5dfa-bf25-723f91b9dfd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472797} :answer-field/id #uuid "25759778-8fb6-5f63-9330-330d39817923" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473793} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c504450c-70b8-5a79-be85-1b4a58e25ce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472798} {:answer/id #uuid "a36721f4-cd73-5f82-8636-041b9bcbe466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a36721f4-cd73-5f82-8636-041b9bcbe466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472799} :answer-field/id #uuid "3db01313-83c9-5e0a-9bc2-aad0155a4cd1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473794} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b78aa730-cf2e-54c8-8191-51cb634845f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472800} {:answer/id #uuid "b01186a6-6a6b-5188-af10-54d4795a3700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b01186a6-6a6b-5188-af10-54d4795a3700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472801} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c46ea6f-2d04-5c7b-a253-b975638bca17" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8147626-87d7-56ca-be09-d1e1490d794e" :question/math-academy-id "q-181667" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A={n\\in Z\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{2})=0}$\n\n- **II.** $B={q\\in Q\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{q\\pi }{2})=0}$\n\n- **III.** $C={x\\in R\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x\\pi }{2})=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\nWe start by finding the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x\\pi }{2})=0$ for $x\\in R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x\\pi }{2} & =m\\pi  \\\\ x & =2m,\\,m\\in Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets:\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the elements of $B$ for different values of $m,$ we have\n\n$$\nA={…,-2,0,2,4,…}.\n$$\n\n- The set $B$ is infinite. Since $A$ is infinite, and $A⊆B,$ it follows that $B$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Since $B$ is infinite, and $B⊆C,$ it follows that $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198271 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26758016-ed47-562a-9338-85c71ffbeaa9" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee82b5b5-8eb7-5ff0-be35-a31c59aea9e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472808} {:answer/id #uuid "60c4e5f8-cc86-5c70-b850-fea2f6e02c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60c4e5f8-cc86-5c70-b850-fea2f6e02c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472809} :answer-field/id #uuid "eab800ab-2c2e-5dc8-b86f-635d0d61cc60" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473799} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88bd4daf-0b70-5425-88e1-3fbe6d0526ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472810} {:answer/id #uuid "c75f52b1-417d-59fb-a71b-22a7249d35f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c75f52b1-417d-59fb-a71b-22a7249d35f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472811} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf48651-9562-59ba-b1ef-9b8d571b7647" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473800} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f84b03a-b49d-5b9d-93fd-ac4bf51bc165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472812} {:answer/id #uuid "9090acca-2e47-5919-9d10-e65cb241a5a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9090acca-2e47-5919-9d10-e65cb241a5a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472813} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cb851b0-1008-559e-bba5-6ac2099260c3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8b98aed-4075-5dac-9091-d486170b806a" :question/math-academy-id "q-181706" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A={{f}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}})\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$\n\n- **II.** $B={{g}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(-\\sqrt{x})\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$\n\n- **III.** $C={{h}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{(0)}(x) & =\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}})=\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}} \\\\ {f}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}})=-\\frac{6}{25\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{8}}} \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}},\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}},-\\frac{6}{25\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{8}}},…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $A$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $B$ is also infinite. Similar to the previous case, listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{(0)}(x) & =-\\sqrt{x} \\\\ {g}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\sqrt{x})=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ {g}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})=\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}} \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nB={-\\sqrt{x},-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}},\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}},…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $C$ is also infinite. Listing a few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{(0)}(x) & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {h}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {h}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})=\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nC={\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}},…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8345ca2e-07d0-5694-85e8-8ac1bcfa3d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474822} {:answer/id #uuid "b5ff36f5-8430-54a9-bec5-2cc165a0f1ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8345ca2e-07d0-5694-85e8-8ac1bcfa3d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474822} :answer-field/id #uuid "df50f4aa-1524-57d2-b1e7-0affdd885093" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "902e3414-ca2a-5ce2-850b-da2dc63be023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474824} {:answer/id #uuid "4e173f75-196d-539f-971b-b9d002b2252d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "902e3414-ca2a-5ce2-850b-da2dc63be023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474824} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4a68604-a5fe-5780-aff3-ee5e03c398ad" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475338} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c276a60-9989-5c94-9ab0-70747f4dd816" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474826} {:answer/id #uuid "50bacac0-c323-5e20-9449-31c6507754e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50bacac0-c323-5e20-9449-31c6507754e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474827} :answer-field/id #uuid "affe140d-4863-54d4-bd0d-1629fd85f31c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2486be8-75b8-51f1-882e-08f8a79961f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42463" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has identical rows\n- **II.** $A$ has proportional columns\n- **III.** $A$ has a zero row\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have proportional columns.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b47a31-7bda-5366-bac4-1d070776e776" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ce9a0ce-3723-5b44-96fb-04d0366dd21f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474620} {:answer/id #uuid "b46dedea-1cf5-5e1a-9cb3-2c020f9a134a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b46dedea-1cf5-5e1a-9cb3-2c020f9a134a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474621} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f4ec09c-15f2-5895-ac80-e0a9327e13e8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475236} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db2e9622-3733-595c-8c9d-874df56fd4e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474622} {:answer/id #uuid "77a1df5c-f867-5e17-b31a-28de951253fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77a1df5c-f867-5e17-b31a-28de951253fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474623} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed2b25fb-534d-5029-9329-43b777f6a7cb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475237} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3138e399-9fd6-5486-a92a-e13b4eda5bb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474624} {:answer/id #uuid "1a41dd38-3d5f-528d-8956-0679daeec641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3138e399-9fd6-5486-a92a-e13b4eda5bb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474624} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c6cb471-5ba9-566a-9280-c3c37963f3a3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5414df0-8556-5960-86b0-386e378b451e" :question/math-academy-id "q-213229" :question/problem "![](images/9c/9cddd6584fee52757b1c7a470a6eeffee3678d569e36025ca70c99e5543c71c2.png)\n\nWhich of the plots above represent a relation, defined on the set $A=\\{\\alpha ,\\beta ,\\delta \\},$ that is neither reflexive nor irreflexive?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nSince $R$ must be neither reflective nor irreflexive, some of the points $(\\alpha ,\\alpha ),$ $(\\beta ,\\beta ),$ and $(\\delta ,\\delta )$ must be in $R,$ and others must not.\n\nThese ordered pairs correspond to the diagonal points on the plots, as shown below:\n\n![](images/7d/7d4257c9e249f9a4c2a53c5566292e21ae6dfa7f0e08e27042548da2d8e7e000.png)\n\n \n\nA plot corresponding to a relation that is neither reflexive nor irreflexive must contain some diagonal points, but not all of them. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198269 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "efdb77bf-dd8b-5ccc-8265-79bd319afaa3" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0da46976-50a0-5bba-a035-84d579bf8c14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474550} {:answer/id #uuid "5cfeed0b-7602-5236-8c0f-9326a62b26c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cfeed0b-7602-5236-8c0f-9326a62b26c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474551} :answer-field/id #uuid "250e3d08-bb55-52da-bcdc-28fa241e7bb6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475201} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b8cefbf-5387-5a3e-b149-b7a67085652a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474552} {:answer/id #uuid "72660f00-03ec-5af3-8cad-aee090d7cc5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b8cefbf-5387-5a3e-b149-b7a67085652a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474552} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c37b18b-100a-5c03-9a73-ee73cbe27f86" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475202} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf8823b7-fb7b-59e1-a6a7-cbae3eb388cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474554} {:answer/id #uuid "0f7216e9-2722-5e5b-a49d-30702f99303c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f7216e9-2722-5e5b-a49d-30702f99303c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474555} :answer-field/id #uuid "76951e29-2db8-583e-baea-5af2220a2cb6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475203}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a7b8c64-0e50-5904-90c5-c8b0f74761de" :question/math-academy-id "q-181771" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A={n\\in Z\\,:\\,-{n}^{2}+n+12\\le 0}$\n\n- **II.** $B={m\\in Z\\,:\\,-{m}^{2}+m+12\\ge 0}$\n\n- **III.** $C={q\\in Q\\,:\\,-{q}^{2}+q+12\\ge 0}$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements. \n\nLet's start by analyzing the parabola $y=-{x}^{2}+x+12$ for $x\\in R.$\n\nFirst, we find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+x+12 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-x-12) & =0 \\\\ -(x-4)(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-3$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](images/57/57d58b579557ba0ea8c6179bd37209c8199eee83e17d79c74828a051aa1382d6.png)\n\nTherefore:\n\n- The solution to the inequality $-{x}^{2}+x+12\\le 0$ for $x\\in R$ is \n\n$$\nx\\le -3\\,\\text{or}\\,x\\ge 4\n$$\n\nand can be expressed as $x\\in {I}_{1}=(-\\infty ,-3]\\cup [4,\\infty ).$\n\n- Similarly, the solution to the inequality $-{x}^{2}+x+12\\ge 0$ for $x\\in R$ is \n\n$$\n-3\\le x\\le 4\n$$\n\nand can be expressed as $x\\in {I}_{2}=[-3,4].$\n\nWith these in mind, let's examine our sets:\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. If $n\\in Z,$ the solutions to the inequality $-{n}^{2}+n+12\\le 0$ are all the integers that lie in the interval ${I}_{1}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nA={…,-4,-3}\\cup {4,5,…}.\n$$\n\n- The set $B$ is finite. If $m\\in Z,$ the solutions to the inequality $-{m}^{2}+m+12\\ge 0$ are all the integers that lie in the interval ${I}_{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nB={-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|B|=8,$ which is finite.\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. If $q\\in Q,$ the solutions to $-{q}^{2}+q+12\\ge 0$ are all the rational numbers that lie in the interval ${I}_{2}.$ Since any real interval of nonzero length contains infinitely many rational numbers, it follows that $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $C$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7345a2-810f-5a35-aa01-092e40df06f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2fbefaa-38d7-5b1f-be3b-d344a924b231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474672} {:answer/id #uuid "3aff4692-6312-58ed-98f2-0a3443f6028f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2fbefaa-38d7-5b1f-be3b-d344a924b231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474672} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7c98675-6c8c-5b6c-81a1-9c741a4b1fef" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17ce5643-56db-5b30-bf6c-3f04636fd51a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474674} {:answer/id #uuid "c65cb16b-cf7f-5925-b88c-a3e129bea8aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c65cb16b-cf7f-5925-b88c-a3e129bea8aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474675} :answer-field/id #uuid "20daba64-8669-59a5-ac11-cb70500da589" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475263} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "617bd55d-af8f-5b9b-b339-9b8aba87ef0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474676} {:answer/id #uuid "02316f99-71bd-5da0-a01a-6cebde20bdbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "617bd55d-af8f-5b9b-b339-9b8aba87ef0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474676} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8022e07-677e-5054-a8ba-974ea9f7d635" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00b6d002-6ca8-5b5f-a710-55bc4f02fb94" :question/math-academy-id "q-216443" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}+7n+12=0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $n\\ge -4$\n- **II.** $n=-4$\n- **III.** $|n|\\le 4$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\n$$\n\nNote that the solutions to the given equation are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+7n+12 & =0 \\\\ (n+4)(n+3) & =0 \\\\ n & =-4,-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n\\ge -4)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=0,$ then $n\\ge -4,$ but ${n}^{2}+7n+12\\ne 0.$\n\n- Condition II is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n=-4)\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $n=-4,$ then ${n}^{2}+7n+12=0.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|n|\\le 4)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=0,$ then $|n|\\le 4,$ but ${n}^{2}+7n+12\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420690 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bc3ecd-2da1-5951-abba-95da02dee826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c974654-2cb6-5b5b-97a1-e7952338aa19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474514} {:answer/id #uuid "77ac130e-f100-51be-bd73-406df515704d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c974654-2cb6-5b5b-97a1-e7952338aa19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474514} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c88976d-d907-52f4-b47a-d7b43494e038" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b124e103-45ef-5879-b034-67056b95ce39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474516} {:answer/id #uuid "ecb1842c-fdd9-5de9-8f9c-62da69dba519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b124e103-45ef-5879-b034-67056b95ce39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474516} :answer-field/id #uuid "0feb969b-f2b9-5a1a-83bd-b7a42fa61e97" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475184} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66d71eb4-f061-5c7b-9f2d-10d55ca0c471" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474518} {:answer/id #uuid "51e51cb2-94cf-54a5-bbf1-cbeee409ec60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51e51cb2-94cf-54a5-bbf1-cbeee409ec60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474519} :answer-field/id #uuid "129babf3-fc18-5e17-9e10-6f9c8b2b5687" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04618c03-3ca0-590d-b082-33d1176f03c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-172300" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}$ is an even number\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $n$ is an odd number\n- **II.** $n$ is a positive number\n- **III.** $n$ is a multiple of $2$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number})\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions. \n\n- Condition I is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number })\\,⇏\\,(n\\text{ is an odd number})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=2$ is not an odd number but ${2}^{2}$ is an even number.\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number})\\,⇏\\,(\\text{ is a positive number})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=-2$ is not a positive number, but $(-2)^{2}$ is an even number.\n\n- Condition III is a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number})\\,⇒\\,(n\\text{ is a multiple of }2)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSince ${n}^{2}$ is even, it must also be true that $n$ is even. Therefore, $n$ is a multiple of $2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7345a2-810f-5a35-aa01-092e40df06f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dea9d9d-31c2-5c01-a455-69465daf1b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474526} {:answer/id #uuid "40fa915d-3313-5401-9881-502282158014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40fa915d-3313-5401-9881-502282158014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474527} :answer-field/id #uuid "17214d23-c467-5173-8f61-0766426c313a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56e611a6-dc82-58ef-8f11-dceebaf58e96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474528} {:answer/id #uuid "0826a1f6-c863-5d42-95b8-1df6c2a6e255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56e611a6-dc82-58ef-8f11-dceebaf58e96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474528} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e223d7b-f377-5bdd-ae40-106ebab7f04d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475190} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc96775f-c6f5-5ca4-9703-f26d24ae7c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474530} {:answer/id #uuid "7f69da4d-9e54-5cfd-923f-6c36718e49e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc96775f-c6f5-5ca4-9703-f26d24ae7c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474530} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1764754-6220-5bd9-aaab-c9961114c472" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10fd92b2-5e05-5850-b7d2-d8140b9fd04f" :question/math-academy-id "q-172315" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}=16$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $n=4$\n- **II.** $-4<n<4$\n- **III.** $|n|<16$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}=16)\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {n}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ (n+4)(n-4) & =0 \\\\ n & =-4,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n=4)\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}=16)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $n=4,$ then ${n}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(-4<n<4)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}=16)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2} & =(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =1\\ne 16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|n|<16)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}=16)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then $|n|<16,$ but ${n}^{2}=1\\ne 16.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7345a2-810f-5a35-aa01-092e40df06f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6918f073-c442-5f18-b455-52622f56f35e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474538} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf41748-06d6-52c6-aa3b-308d83a706dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6918f073-c442-5f18-b455-52622f56f35e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474538} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d8263b8-7e82-5b77-9f03-bec084e88fd5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475195} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9e39ef7-a88b-577a-b0d6-705ea2d526fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474540} {:answer/id #uuid "87a04c93-3149-5e28-8454-384821f8c32e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87a04c93-3149-5e28-8454-384821f8c32e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474541} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2fed408-cdcd-55a9-a9f4-12abd80bada2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475196} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e26f992c-0caf-597a-b322-2e782bc69db1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474542} {:answer/id #uuid "88843fa6-1855-53ff-af9a-14a6b6a49357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88843fa6-1855-53ff-af9a-14a6b6a49357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474543} :answer-field/id #uuid "2accb876-bb81-5087-87aa-41721160c992" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "28567992-ba7f-5623-ad07-13abe4be416c" :question/math-academy-id "q-172325" :question/problem "$\\,$ $x+1>4$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $|x|>3$\n- **II.** $x>3$\n- **III.** $x>4$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,(x+1>4)\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & >4 \\\\ x & >3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|x|>3)\\,⇏\\,(x+1>4)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-4,$ then we have $x+1=-3≯4.$\n\n- Condition II is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(x>3)\\,⇒\\,(x+1>4)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $x>3,$ then $x+1>4.$\n\n- Condition III is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(x>4)\\,⇒\\,(x+1>4)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $x>4,$ then  $x+1>5>4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "655a0356-bbf0-5769-86d7-6674c65d0f87" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22fd7e43-5c76-592b-aee4-f521964cb28a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474690} {:answer/id #uuid "56db8c6a-3927-5f57-8d4a-f66704069758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22fd7e43-5c76-592b-aee4-f521964cb28a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474690} :answer-field/id #uuid "5591e25a-3ea8-5f89-9be5-e954600bbcf0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475271} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aaacbae-01bd-5b78-b909-ba34f4a8bfe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474692} {:answer/id #uuid "9df9fb08-bffb-50d9-9054-b845a6a759d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0aaacbae-01bd-5b78-b909-ba34f4a8bfe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474692} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3b5576e-92d4-5f62-a180-abf1cc0efd81" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475272} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a32688b-9a6e-5531-97e4-13b963ffda66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474694} {:answer/id #uuid "65d2bf31-d717-50e7-9174-4e253ccf20e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65d2bf31-d717-50e7-9174-4e253ccf20e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474695} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd972e0-15e5-5c38-b69b-4c566a479a6a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "390cc44c-87e5-5905-81de-8b4495a342fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-216459" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n- **I.** $f$ is a differentiable function\n- **II.** $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$\n- **III.** $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C,$ for any $C\\in R$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C\\in R$ is the arbitrary constant.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇍\\,(f\\text{ is a differentiable function})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the function $f(x)={e}^{x}$ is a differentiable function but ${f}^{′}(x)\\ne {sec}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇏\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, for the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1,$ the statement ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ is true but $f(x)\\ne \\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1.$\n\n- Condition III is both necessary and sufficient: The statement ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ is true *if and only if* $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C,$ for any $C\\in R.$\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇒\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇐\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇔\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bc3ecd-2da1-5951-abba-95da02dee826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a89bb0c-0c7b-56f1-b539-37a12390f125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474520} {:answer/id #uuid "6ae93c4e-dbee-5e05-a6c8-d9c42170ca16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ae93c4e-dbee-5e05-a6c8-d9c42170ca16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474521} :answer-field/id #uuid "ead4a86f-a7fe-5af4-9eb4-5b3a0b8b20db" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e692d5a-6355-5a16-ad53-70eaf6632af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474522} {:answer/id #uuid "a6f1e8fb-2da6-5ee5-9d4d-1da86e369e4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e692d5a-6355-5a16-ad53-70eaf6632af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474522} :answer-field/id #uuid "f94fd077-0724-53df-91f5-264867194b12" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475187} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6518693-7320-54ee-9d17-34a1c0cb7d16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474524} {:answer/id #uuid "f2f11120-7136-5045-b049-91d280b83ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6518693-7320-54ee-9d17-34a1c0cb7d16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474524} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd17e2ae-aab3-52ac-be51-99890d5d4e21" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b376045-26da-55cb-becc-db924f8d2dac" :question/math-academy-id "q-172302" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}$ is an odd number\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $n$ is odd\n- **II.** $n$ is a multiple of $3$\n- **III.** $n$ is a multiple of $5$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an odd number})\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions. \n\n- Condition I is a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an odd number})\\,⇒\\,(\\text{ }n\\text{ is odd})\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSince ${n}^{2}$ is odd, it must also be true that $n$ is odd.\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an odd number})\\,⇏\\,(n\\text{ is a multiple of }3)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=7$ is not a multiple of $3,$ but ${n}^{2}=49$ is an odd number.\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an odd number})\\,⇏\\,(n\\text{ is a multiple of }5)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=9$ is not a multiple of $5,$ but ${n}^{2}=81$ is an odd number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "655a0356-bbf0-5769-86d7-6674c65d0f87" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "275eb9b3-6e5b-5c62-98b4-03f5eb30ad04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474684} {:answer/id #uuid "3d1d7d46-08e9-5f82-8332-0c08cdf016f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "275eb9b3-6e5b-5c62-98b4-03f5eb30ad04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474684} :answer-field/id #uuid "43cd0fdc-7d67-5615-af44-f39feac6c9d7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475268} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f543881f-8b99-5c13-b785-3641b1d5fb06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474686} {:answer/id #uuid "2882d536-f3b4-518b-b85a-785eed089933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2882d536-f3b4-518b-b85a-785eed089933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474687} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eb42275-1db2-5292-815e-e65c000092bf" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5589a6d5-b7d4-5595-bff4-bffeea5bfecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474688} {:answer/id #uuid "7ee035f5-77ee-597c-89c2-301f34f633df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5589a6d5-b7d4-5595-bff4-bffeea5bfecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474688} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b4b9e5b-d610-515d-8a2a-ae5777bcd975" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5904ff03-6479-54c0-a38b-31e73684000e" :question/math-academy-id "q-216449" :question/problem "$\\,$ $12∣x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n- **I.** $2∣x$ and $6∣x$\n- **II.** $3∣x$ and $4∣x$\n- **III.** $3∣x$ and $8∣x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇍\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }6∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=6$ is divisible by $2$ and by $6$ but not divisible by $12.$\n\n- Condition II is both necessary and sufficient: A number is divisible by $12$ *if and only if* it's divisible by both $3$ and $4.$\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇒\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }4∣x)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇐\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }4∣x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇔\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }4∣x)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇏\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }8∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=12$ is divisible by $12$ but not divisible by $8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bc3ecd-2da1-5951-abba-95da02dee826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e2e3884-4256-5fcd-a5d4-dadd9c5c4fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474508} {:answer/id #uuid "99a25cfb-7af1-584e-a23f-07d1873c1ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e2e3884-4256-5fcd-a5d4-dadd9c5c4fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474508} :answer-field/id #uuid "16abb1e1-f335-5e47-9697-b110c37be556" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caf8abdb-a012-5e69-b701-8cd5c59400ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474510} {:answer/id #uuid "00e746e6-7edf-5a02-bac0-109198a72497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00e746e6-7edf-5a02-bac0-109198a72497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474511} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b5cd708-41b4-5971-b4bb-2aec404fccd4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475181} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73900034-e9c8-5e7c-87af-8e3c53f25b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474512} {:answer/id #uuid "1149f043-cd71-50ca-9599-b2751718dde1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73900034-e9c8-5e7c-87af-8e3c53f25b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474512} :answer-field/id #uuid "471b8d11-4b50-5b5b-ba37-b436e873213e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ef2cacc-c405-55b2-8430-66b58129ad71" :question/math-academy-id "q-172298" :question/problem "$\\,$ $|x-2|=6$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $x>4$\n- **II.** $|x|<10$\n- **III.** $x=8$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n(|x-2|=6)\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x-2| & =6 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 6 \\\\ x & =-4,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(|x-2|=6)\\,⇏\\,(x>4)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-4,$ then $|x-2|=6,$ but $x≯4.$\n\n- Condition II is a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(|x-2|=6)\\,⇒\\,(|x|<10)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nEach solution of $|x-2|=6$ satisfies $|x|<10.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(|x-2|=6)\\,⇏\\,(x=8)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-4,$ then $|x-2|=6,$ but $x\\ne 8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "655a0356-bbf0-5769-86d7-6674c65d0f87" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2f333be-b379-55db-a2cb-5b230d6296ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474574} {:answer/id #uuid "a5279a66-07ec-57a7-bb9e-535e8ba78ac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2f333be-b379-55db-a2cb-5b230d6296ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474574} :answer-field/id #uuid "27f4abd5-a94c-52bf-9770-c5e45fbe660c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7f67d93-7ed5-5d39-8f29-efe5dd8fbcd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474576} {:answer/id #uuid "cec0961f-126b-58ac-a00e-2aecea8918ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cec0961f-126b-58ac-a00e-2aecea8918ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474577} :answer-field/id #uuid "7540f77e-125b-5cdf-a8c9-e205ca0e22bb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475214} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b77f3b1-66c6-54d7-b4cf-6918eacddddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474578} {:answer/id #uuid "8298e019-7f7f-55ad-bd6d-8f876ec7a351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b77f3b1-66c6-54d7-b4cf-6918eacddddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474578} :answer-field/id #uuid "94175714-0186-5f94-b2de-ff35a6a19b00" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e1662ac-5299-5cc7-92ca-68567f121fc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-183429" :question/problem "$\\,$ $20∣x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n- **I.** $2∣x$ and $10∣x$\n- **II.** $4∣x$ and $5∣x$\n- **III.** $100∣x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇍\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }10∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=10$ is divisible by $2$ and by $10$ but not divisible by $20.$\n\n- Condition II is both necessary and sufficient: A number is divisible by $20$ *if and only if* it's divisible by both $4$ and $5.$\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇒\\,(4∣x\\text{ and }5∣x)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇐\\,(4∣x\\text{ and }5∣x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇔\\,(4∣x\\text{ and }5∣x)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇏\\,(100∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=20$ is divisible by $20$ but not divisible by $100.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420700 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "655a0356-bbf0-5769-86d7-6674c65d0f87" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb05016-ebc2-5387-8920-8f619655786a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474588} {:answer/id #uuid "48b8b3ed-0f8f-5b6d-8216-a969149d45a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cb05016-ebc2-5387-8920-8f619655786a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474588} :answer-field/id #uuid "5929b0d4-9f53-5302-b541-d4a631026b05" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475220} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "320e0268-bb47-5058-9d07-2b67422add47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474590} {:answer/id #uuid "f7571c42-2ed9-58a2-ac68-52195ba3461e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7571c42-2ed9-58a2-ac68-52195ba3461e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474591} :answer-field/id #uuid "df033f1c-530a-5163-8431-c2cdfe6cba01" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475221} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dc295db-adb7-5a03-aa88-578d033a6fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474592} {:answer/id #uuid "7fc133e0-ab07-5ef0-aa15-ee3ec0ef27d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dc295db-adb7-5a03-aa88-578d033a6fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474592} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5e2035c-abbc-53ab-9142-02378bf8a91d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475222}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9dd0c0c2-7652-5690-ae78-53d067f574fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-183485" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(x)=2$\n- **II.** $f(x)={x}^{2}+C,$ for any $C\\in R$\n- **III.** $f(x)={x}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int 2x\\,dx \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C\\in R$ is the arbitrary constant.\n\nMoreover, the differential equation ${f}^{″}(x)=2$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\int 2\\,dx \\\\  & =2x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D\\in R$ is another arbitrary constant.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇍\\,({f}^{″}(x)=2)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, for the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+x,$ we have ${f}^{′}(x)=2x+1,$ and so the statement ${f}^{″}(x)=2$  is true but ${f}^{′}(x)\\ne 2x.$\n\n- Condition II is both necessary and sufficient: The statement ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$ is true *if and only if* $f(x)={x}^{2}+C,$ for any $C\\in R.$\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇒\\,(f(x)={x}^{2}+C)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇐\\,(f(x)={x}^{2}+C).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇔\\,(f(x)={x}^{2}+C)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇏\\,(f(x)={x}^{2})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, for the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+1$ the statement ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$ is true but $f(x)\\ne {x}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7345a2-810f-5a35-aa01-092e40df06f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "408df0cb-6c6f-5d9b-90f1-7f582171bc71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474532} {:answer/id #uuid "e8c3c23c-90bd-53c4-815e-4acbcce6f3e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8c3c23c-90bd-53c4-815e-4acbcce6f3e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474533} :answer-field/id #uuid "c650a4e4-46df-5663-8cc8-623efe286c07" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9112523-8587-5ffa-8287-6ac21dbb9e74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474534} {:answer/id #uuid "d42bf337-0cdd-5dad-902c-9e538740fc05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d42bf337-0cdd-5dad-902c-9e538740fc05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474535} :answer-field/id #uuid "03bb3ee9-bab8-5ebf-9f70-e330a2b233ff" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475193} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5ba5bf5-e61c-5fb1-91c6-c2c59dbcaad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474536} {:answer/id #uuid "fa034870-2511-553a-a643-bf518efcae8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5ba5bf5-e61c-5fb1-91c6-c2c59dbcaad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474536} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d785b52-fdd9-556d-a378-0f57be058f85" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e4cdd56d-10e6-5abf-be98-585e1ce87428" :question/math-academy-id "q-172322" :question/problem "$\\,$ $a\\ge 10$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $a=10$\n- **II.** $a>15$\n- **III.** $a>5$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,(a\\ge 10)\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(a=10)\\,⇒\\,(a\\ge 10)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $a=10,$ then $a\\ge 10.$\n\n- Condition II is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(a>15)\\,⇒\\,(a\\ge 10)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $a>15,$ then $a\\ge 10.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(a>5)\\,⇏\\,(a\\ge 10)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $a=7,$ then we have $a≱10.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bc3ecd-2da1-5951-abba-95da02dee826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ebae4c6-911d-5b7a-81a5-489639363761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474666} {:answer/id #uuid "37584277-dd5a-53f8-ab90-99bca0e04e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ebae4c6-911d-5b7a-81a5-489639363761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474666} :answer-field/id #uuid "27021643-f42e-5623-ae73-432d54977b4f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475259} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "902a3cbf-5052-5b08-8b8e-6c65dbb7c4b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474668} {:answer/id #uuid "ed4980a6-395d-529f-a3bc-ec28c85a6476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed4980a6-395d-529f-a3bc-ec28c85a6476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474669} :answer-field/id #uuid "916ce97d-4d5e-523b-92f1-ff944d43f48b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475260} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "739985f7-aa1a-505d-8792-e69101c7b41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474670} {:answer/id #uuid "c76a103a-9ee1-57f6-8fb2-89f461de2bab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "739985f7-aa1a-505d-8792-e69101c7b41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474670} :answer-field/id #uuid "207c9ae9-3188-5600-be34-4699d2e652f0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ed1378b7-d665-5e7d-b9bb-42ac28cb1db4" :question/math-academy-id "q-216436" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $x({x}^{2}+x-6)\\le 0$\n- **II.** $x\\le 2$\n- **III.** $x\\ge 0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0)\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given inequality is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-6 & \\le 0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-2) & \\le 0 \\\\ -3\\le x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0)\\,⇏\\,(x({x}^{2}+x-6)\\le 0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-1,$ then ${x}^{2}+x-6=-6\\le 0,$ but $x({x}^{2}+x-6)=6≰0.$\n\n- Condition II is a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0)\\,⇒\\,(x\\le 2)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nEvery solution of ${x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0$ satisfies $x\\le 2.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0)\\,⇏\\,(x\\ge 0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-1,$ then ${x}^{2}+x-6=-6\\le 0,$ but $x≱0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "655a0356-bbf0-5769-86d7-6674c65d0f87" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee9221a1-9cab-59c0-bf56-6f848a7e0e48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474678} {:answer/id #uuid "c3cf31c3-f73e-5d77-b53d-a8d455c7cff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3cf31c3-f73e-5d77-b53d-a8d455c7cff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474679} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c70687e-b308-5f84-8a15-0e5dd9994cdb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475265} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a52e76-808e-5123-a481-05236f391726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474680} {:answer/id #uuid "0dcf35a2-41a1-5a2a-9a10-98ec347c21fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12a52e76-808e-5123-a481-05236f391726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474680} :answer-field/id #uuid "5089e15d-deca-5a6e-aece-72b0f44cadea" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475266} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6b07157-b267-5eaa-9880-368af70fa7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474682} {:answer/id #uuid "73ad770f-d82f-590b-919c-e6168b3b87ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6b07157-b267-5eaa-9880-368af70fa7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474682} :answer-field/id #uuid "d95c6284-4027-528a-ae0b-3b8935544bfd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475267}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f653d451-6beb-59b1-affd-6d539e9553ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-216447" :question/problem "$\\,$ $18∣x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n- **I.** $2∣x$ and $9∣x$\n- **II.** $3∣x$ and $6∣x$\n- **III.** $72∣x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is both necessary and sufficient: A number is divisible by $18$ *if and only if* it's divisible by both $2$ and $9.$\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇒\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }9∣x)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇐\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }9∣x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇔\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }9∣x)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇍\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }6∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=6$ is divisible by $3$ and by $6$ but not divisible by $18.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇏\\,(72∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=18$ is divisible by $18$ but not divisible by $72.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b7b8782-d1f4-5654-a18f-6ad35de8fb30" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Flux's Sign From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1e6a479-52d1-5ae4-939a-e3b5d03fd778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474284} {:answer/id #uuid "4890dcc8-ff49-5248-a3fb-0fe1da9aeb4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1e6a479-52d1-5ae4-939a-e3b5d03fd778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474284} :answer-field/id #uuid "f527906f-2d30-55d6-998b-e4e8bf90fc09" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb84b4f7-0bc5-5c5a-9056-122bbc70bc57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474286} {:answer/id #uuid "cc9a6aa9-acc4-5992-a14e-804d5a9c01a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb84b4f7-0bc5-5c5a-9056-122bbc70bc57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474286} :answer-field/id #uuid "65cb578f-78b5-5225-966a-db5a469b668e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475069} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fac217d6-6ce8-5003-9d34-2c9ea1c6c89d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474288} {:answer/id #uuid "bcc8acfa-931e-5f66-bebf-19feca6c0ef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcc8acfa-931e-5f66-bebf-19feca6c0ef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474289} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d35692f-6bb0-56b8-9a68-82c51fb3c32c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ae03bac-e2a8-5c3b-a5da-8c8f23590a03" :question/math-academy-id "q-127026" :question/problem "![](images/28/28a7eb32cfcd800c907e9f4af927eca7bd8616d36162682413db62a9feabefbb.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is negative\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nTo understand the flux intuitively, we imagine that $F$ represents a stream of flowing water. The flux of $F$ across $C$ represents the net flow of water escaping the region bounded by $C:$ \n\n- If more water flows out through $C$ than in through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *out* through $C$), the flux is *positive*.\n\n- If more water flows in through $C$ than out through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *in* through $C$), the flux is *negative*.\n\n![](images/a7/a72dc9866562a42a49590fd169424307675b2c14b36833bd729026f46b677eec.png)\n\n- If the net flow through $C$ is zero then the flux equals zero.\n\n![](images/3a/3a6ac8656b2e0b5cc482a16eb3a4fab57cb681c9a40cf634da47f9a4323d9fdf.png)\n\nFor an arbitrary closed curve, the outward-pointing unit normal vector tells us which direction is \"out.\"\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. From the diagram below it's clear that there is a net flow *out* through $C.$ \n\n![](images/fe/fecf59674259d41222ffd981b1ab6d90c474fe2b0e37a6d5f7626f34536a6896.png)\n\nTherefore, the flux is positive, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. When measuring flux through a closed curve, the orientation of the curve does not matter because the outward-pointing unit normal vector is the same at each point on $C$ in either case.\n\n![](images/56/56a7fc09ed2a2a15b0949fa6041dc9c0ee6beb69f30b1a5c048afd8c57887d52.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{-C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b7b8782-d1f4-5654-a18f-6ad35de8fb30" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Flux's Sign From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2126782-b8eb-539b-8a44-4b656f8cdc89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474278} {:answer/id #uuid "bc560dd6-7ac6-5a76-9df4-70c53f25e56e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2126782-b8eb-539b-8a44-4b656f8cdc89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474278} :answer-field/id #uuid "94621230-a9f0-50e7-b575-e0567a8c5e06" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475065} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43e5a016-6e60-5487-bdda-a02e34603edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474280} {:answer/id #uuid "52b18bb0-cfb3-5c9f-948f-ea3749f36b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52b18bb0-cfb3-5c9f-948f-ea3749f36b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474281} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5d370b0-1e92-5c62-966f-578bba64458f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475066} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "137d1b3d-a1ad-5c7d-a87f-d48c60a7cbf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474282} {:answer/id #uuid "6c50f32b-3afd-545c-a6cd-342f755fc462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "137d1b3d-a1ad-5c7d-a87f-d48c60a7cbf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474282} :answer-field/id #uuid "3241e849-1133-58ff-a9e9-26f068ba66c0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1cc7cc51-6281-53f8-b74f-55c2a0b2fa6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127024" :question/problem "![](images/01/01d8d85064253b9241b1fd93c22381897f23556d6e02c5c2c0161c94cee3bbdf.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is negative\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nTo understand the flux intuitively, we imagine that $F$ represents a stream of flowing water. The flux of $F$ across $C$ represents the net flow of water escaping the region bounded by $C:$ \n\n- If more water flows out through $C$ than in through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *out* through $C$), the flux is *positive*.\n\n- If more water flows in through $C$ than out through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *in* through $C$), the flux is *negative*.\n\n![](images/a7/a72dc9866562a42a49590fd169424307675b2c14b36833bd729026f46b677eec.png)\n\n- If the net flow through $C$ is zero then the flux equals zero.\n\n![](images/3a/3a6ac8656b2e0b5cc482a16eb3a4fab57cb681c9a40cf634da47f9a4323d9fdf.png)\n\nFor an arbitrary closed curve, the outward-pointing unit normal vector tells us which direction is \"out.\"\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. From the diagram below it's clear that there is a net flow *in* through $C.$ \n\n![](images/bb/bb4fd4068760bb9132052b26508f0e1e0c02c45d425770de804b17ce7c512919.png)\n\nTherefore, the flux is negative, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. When measuring flux through a closed curve, the orientation of the curve does not matter because the outward-pointing unit normal vector is the same at each point on $C$ in either case.\n\n![](images/46/46afd4cde01c95388c9daefbef0668ef696d5817ab9ea3614982edf58a9bdf55.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $-C$ is negative, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{-C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s<0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b7b8782-d1f4-5654-a18f-6ad35de8fb30" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Flux's Sign From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86148950-3fc2-5f38-81ce-53ec93e76166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474290} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c0a1d4-d321-51db-9f9a-4313b742971e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86148950-3fc2-5f38-81ce-53ec93e76166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474290} :answer-field/id #uuid "eff65640-e27c-5010-a702-518eac2480f9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa09f0c0-3016-5c6e-b7c4-55a245d9d0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474292} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c0e836-a991-5f1a-91a3-7effd835eb73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0c0e836-a991-5f1a-91a3-7effd835eb73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474293} :answer-field/id #uuid "176d727d-d760-55bb-bfd3-626eda4dc691" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475072} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7817b13e-8e9a-530f-860c-d01aa3b29a65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474294} {:answer/id #uuid "419f49db-2832-5c8c-8fb3-49f7638b7dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "419f49db-2832-5c8c-8fb3-49f7638b7dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474295} :answer-field/id #uuid "912976bb-a0fa-5d56-b533-8354e5ec824a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e18756f-1e50-5f09-be71-26f001c4f68e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127027" :question/problem "![](images/af/afaec113101f1a63134d2b1cb5c9744b93f9b84dabafaa205780d2dc5b49a7bc.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is positive\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nTo understand the flux intuitively, we imagine that $F$ represents a stream of flowing water. The flux of $F$ across $C$ represents the net flow of water escaping the region bounded by $C:$ \n\n- If more water flows out through $C$ than in through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *out* through $C$), the flux is *positive*.\n\n- If more water flows in through $C$ than out through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *in* through $C$), the flux is *negative*.\n\n![](images/a7/a72dc9866562a42a49590fd169424307675b2c14b36833bd729026f46b677eec.png)\n\n- If the net flow through $C$ is zero then the flux equals zero.\n\n![](images/3a/3a6ac8656b2e0b5cc482a16eb3a4fab57cb681c9a40cf634da47f9a4323d9fdf.png)\n\nFor an arbitrary closed curve, the outward-pointing unit normal vector tells us which direction is \"out.\"\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. From the diagram below it's clear that there is a net flow *out* through $C.$ \n\n![](images/6b/6b24ece279cc480f20d7a4dbc65f7a5257af71f22688b1416c73e3b40673a321.png)\n\nTherefore, the flux is positive, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. When measuring flux through a closed curve, the orientation of the curve does not matter because the outward-pointing unit normal vector is the same at each point on $C$ in either case.\n\n![](images/9e/9e8527d26f0f2bd5372d8643f8f9321ec022bb0079e1fc5b23be4978f436613c.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{-C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b7b8782-d1f4-5654-a18f-6ad35de8fb30" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Flux's Sign From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fc352a7-def2-5836-9338-8008f169268f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474296} {:answer/id #uuid "3d7131d4-fc3c-5f44-9a24-a7c8c38852ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d7131d4-fc3c-5f44-9a24-a7c8c38852ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474297} :answer-field/id #uuid "72b3e34c-4c68-5a6b-8479-025af4a4eb97" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475074} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "367f3fa0-3258-53ba-b118-21195c91f07c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474298} {:answer/id #uuid "8135c933-85bc-5657-aea9-2ece1f6a47c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "367f3fa0-3258-53ba-b118-21195c91f07c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474298} :answer-field/id #uuid "91409016-0963-5d73-b7be-10a1f16408c7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475075} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd98a563-23aa-5acb-89d3-93294ee5cc96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474300} {:answer/id #uuid "60ef0350-a526-513b-87b0-99da9194b0ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd98a563-23aa-5acb-89d3-93294ee5cc96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474300} :answer-field/id #uuid "17b07bc2-ae25-563c-8ed2-caa1721146f6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "765f030b-c4cb-527c-8c26-c947b0ace6a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-127028" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f1d25942ae680c068b587f38bfbc968c8850b8fa2db2003e994e1ec32dad892.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is positive\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is negative\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nTo understand the flux intuitively, we imagine that $F$ represents a stream of flowing water. The flux of $F$ across $C$ represents the net flow of water escaping the region bounded by $C:$ \n\n- If more water flows out through $C$ than in through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *out* through $C$), the flux is *positive*.\n\n- If more water flows in through $C$ than out through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *in* through $C$), the flux is *negative*.\n\n![](images/a7/a72dc9866562a42a49590fd169424307675b2c14b36833bd729026f46b677eec.png)\n\n- If the net flow through $C$ is zero then the flux equals zero.\n\n![](images/3a/3a6ac8656b2e0b5cc482a16eb3a4fab57cb681c9a40cf634da47f9a4323d9fdf.png)\n\nFor an arbitrary closed curve, the outward-pointing unit normal vector tells us which direction is \"out.\"\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Note that the flux $F$ that flows in through $C$ is the same that flows out through $C.$ Therefore, there is no net flow of $F$ through $C.$\n\n![](images/b7/b7acc3028de66ae71ae4e425da639e51a357a77f2b0a345290592cac91ba17d3.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. When measuring flux through a closed curve, the orientation of the curve does not matter because the outward-pointing unit normal vector is the same at each point on $C$ in either case.\n\n![](images/04/04639a0074aa4607fa57bfe589aad1780f8da6f573d8589a68c2fdb569b5a129.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $-C$ is zero, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{-C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "977dd536-4220-524b-931c-3ba60f55073d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474556} {:answer/id #uuid "48cbd00d-6155-5f97-ad98-53542fd4bb4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "977dd536-4220-524b-931c-3ba60f55073d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474556} :answer-field/id #uuid "251277cb-3ad8-5af9-897f-6f40b45fce72" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475204} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c59c1ac2-aac3-545b-8f90-1ae8a978cafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474558} {:answer/id #uuid "741d8b65-925b-5a70-8aff-77354bc69797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c59c1ac2-aac3-545b-8f90-1ae8a978cafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474558} :answer-field/id #uuid "d170f76e-4e31-5ac5-b1a2-1881ac8d197d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475205} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffc21ad4-56fc-56ad-8058-de8c73d359e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474560} {:answer/id #uuid "4843b0fb-74a8-5c2c-b516-cacac8678dd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4843b0fb-74a8-5c2c-b516-cacac8678dd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474561} :answer-field/id #uuid "254e65e2-d3aa-5440-89cf-3f8963043077" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c44203d-f0c3-504e-a004-3addf0955223" :question/math-academy-id "q-181956" :question/problem "If $A=\\{-2,2\\}$ and $B=\\{c,d\\},$ which of the following elements belong to $(A\\times B)\\times B?$\n\nI. $(-2,d,c)$\n\nII. $(-2,(c,d))$\n\nIII. $((2,d),c)$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${-2,2}$ with ${c,d},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/98/98e7cfca515290b952ea5aefc9b2516a5cd6a68de0dc048c2075128e6c60b651.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(-2,c),(-2,d),(2,c),(2,d)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\n(A\\times B)\\times B\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $A\\times B$ and $B,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/1e/1e96aeb1c5bfb1f9faa590a8eb8b01528a1ce9431a3f1ceac92b156a9bdde221.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|(A\\times B)\\times B|=|A\\times B|\\cdot |B|=4\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $((2,d),c)\\in (A\\times B)\\times B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] 