:question/math-academy-id "q-214252" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $N.$\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,y∤x\n$$\n\n Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $R$ is reflexive\n- **II.** $R$ is symmetric\n- **III.** $R$ is transitive\n- **IV.** $R$ is an equivalence relation\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is not reflexive. For example, $3∣3.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not symmetric. For example, $9∤3$ but $3∣9.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not transitive. For example, $3∤2$ and $2∤9,$ but $3∣9.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not an equivalence relation since it's neither reflexive nor symmetric nor transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56e1a8e8-e6fa-5d18-a8ea-e9b55d53facb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474644} {:answer/id #uuid "a170fea6-c960-5d28-8f6b-a9fccc84dc24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56e1a8e8-e6fa-5d18-a8ea-e9b55d53facb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/i