tion/id #uuid "78aa39d2-6d95-5a7b-bd86-1b4658d3d903" :question/math-academy-id "q-214247" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are equivalence relations on $Q?$\n- **I.** $x\\,R\\,y$ if ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4$\n- **II.** $x=y$\n- **III.** $x\\,R\\,y$ if $xy\\in N$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- Relation I is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because ${2}^{2}+{2}^{2}≰4.$\n\n- Relation II is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\n- Relation III is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\notin N.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90b7f96d-2c26-51b8-a503-b732dd7105e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474638} {:answer/id #uuid "58fade47-8b11-5fab-b25b-851ce73bce58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58fade47-8b11-5fab-b25b-851ce73bce58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474639} :answer-field/id #uuid "4680e212-67d2-5252-a922-ef475a60beba" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b7d6869-692f-5caa-9e55-9630f69a0c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474640} {:answer/id #uuid "39b3b2e0-da86-5014-bd8a-ee945f0ebf31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b7d6869-692f-5caa-9e55-9630f69a0c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474640} :answer-field/id #uuid "1378d38d-6558-5839-92ba-4bd5499dd871" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475246} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b0ed5c9-e5e6-562a-8122-0bb3e30b37ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474642} {:answer/id #uuid "b94689af-dc54-597e-8c18-94f6e4db05f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b0ed5c9-e5e6-562a-8122-0bb3e30b37ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474642} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b62643e-bd65-5cdf-a6f5-99efc18252aa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a3f6ced1-e3e7-51b2-bdb3-c0561413aee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-214246" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are equivalence relations on $N?$\n- **I.** $a\\,R\\,b$ if $a-b$ is a multiple of $2$\n- **II.** $a∣b$\n- **III.** $a\\,R\\,b$ if $3∣(a+b)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- Relation I is an equivalence relation. \n\n- It is reflexive because for all $a\\in N,$ we have that $a-a=0$ is a multiple of $2.$\n\n- It is symmetric because for all $a,b\\in N,$ if $a-b$ is a multiple of $2,$ then $b-a$ is also a multiple of $2.$\n\n- It is transitive because for all $a,b,c\\in N,$ if $a-b$ is a multiple of $2$ and $b-c$ is a multiple of $2,$ then\n\n$$\na-c=(a-b)+(b-c)\n$$\n\nis also a multiple of $2.$\n\n- Relation II is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not symmetric since $3∣6$ but $6∤3.$\n\n- Relation III is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive since $3∤(1+1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421484 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3888085d-918f-58a3-8bd9-367a97d32018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474562} {:answer/id #uuid "3e335ed9-b0c7-50b7-bf4b-dc3aedd3cf2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3888085d-918f-58a3-8bd9-367a97d32018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474562} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e29da06-bfce-529c-931f-97c2357fe6fc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475207} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad121aa6-d319-5297-af2a-e5e3093bb81a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474564} {:answer/id #uuid "c0be6723-f4cc-55bc-99d0-0ee75e7b4417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0be6723-f4cc-55bc-99d0-0ee75e7b4417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474565} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b29ca3-f143-548a-ae89-a64c0ea33837" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd45a65d-0d13-5724-926d-fad0cc9c4e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474566} {:answer/id #uuid "822c7061-50fc-56dd-a5fd-3acb6e1d930d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "822c7061-50fc-56dd-a5fd-3acb6e1d930d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474567} :answer-field/id #uuid "ace444cf-7548-524c-92d8-dd3be4616e9d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd7d0702-ab54-5763-af3c-93c657eacc9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-181974" :question/problem "If $A=\\{1,2,3\\}$ and $B=\\{x,y\\},$ which of the following elements belong to $(B\\times B)\\times A?$\n\nI. $(x,y,1)$\n\nII. $((x,x),1)$\n\nIII. $((y,x),2)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $B\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${x,y}$ with ${x,y},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/5a/5af389ab817ce509519af7a3c1a5fdbb583d8e13859b9aa3b6166958f81e3040.png)\n\nHence, the set $B\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nB\\times B={(x,x),(x,y),(y,x),(y,y)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|B\\times B|=|B|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\n(B\\times B)\\times A\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $B\\times B$ and $A,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/da/dae7febad357be8d9f000c9dc7abfbe97fda34e3e9ff0b0e8ab0289e3c4e782a.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|(B\\times B)\\times A|=|B\\times B|\\cdot |A|=4\\cdot 3=12.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $((x,x),1)$ and $((y,x),2)$ are in $(B\\times B)\\times A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3601ac83-0800-567a-9a0d-4d5c37cef413" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to an Equivalence Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8fb2458-5f62-526c-a4ef-234eebfd2a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474870} {:answer/id #uuid "dedf894e-8578-5838-bb97-a01a04d5b043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8fb2458-5f62-526c-a4ef-234eebfd2a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474870} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5e50a82-11c9-5ec6-83f0-10556f882d83" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475361} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f08c149-5209-5a09-b35d-403519f5bb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474872} {:answer/id #uuid "2bdc995a-9e19-5d0b-8013-21abcf455610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f08c149-5209-5a09-b35d-403519f5bb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474872} :answer-field/id #uuid "817fe686-a8a8-5d25-a62f-e53303899546" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee2df81f-2ec6-525a-a134-5bba469a3318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474874} {:answer/id #uuid "d585ca0c-899d-5058-8710-6692be7979a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d585ca0c-899d-5058-8710-6692be7979a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474875} :answer-field/id #uuid "d662e169-3539-5ca6-8143-0749449a329b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "071418af-96d7-52c9-8845-42c31b88cc12" :question/math-academy-id "q-77200" :question/problem "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $R,$ defined by $x∼y$ if ${x}^{3}={y}^{3}.$ Which of the following are in the equivalence class $[8]?$\n\nI. $-2$\n\nII. $2$\n\nIII. $8$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The equivalence class $[8]$ consists of the elements that are equivalent to $8$ under the given equivalence relation. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[8] & ={x\\in R\\,|\\,x∼8} \\\\  & ={x\\in R\\,|\\,{x}^{3}={8}^{3}} \\\\  & ={x\\in R\\,|\\,x=8} \\\\  & ={8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $8$ is in $[8],$ while $-2$ and $2$ are not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3601ac83-0800-567a-9a0d-4d5c37cef413" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to an Equivalence Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ffea43b-d86a-56b6-bcdb-ce67bcdc018f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474702} {:answer/id #uuid "d2529ebd-b8d8-5045-af24-d984f85479f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2529ebd-b8d8-5045-af24-d984f85479f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474703} :answer-field/id #uuid "45da432d-dfec-5baf-8401-8d2846f1d77c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e71abca-c9a3-5770-8721-0722ffcda4d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474704} {:answer/id #uuid "d573ebbe-f7e5-5ea5-8330-54a24a3ef9bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e71abca-c9a3-5770-8721-0722ffcda4d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474704} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e233bb6-7ce4-57bc-a294-bd1bb72c0ce4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e537730-288f-53d7-b55a-154f5a93b6c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474706} {:answer/id #uuid "aa9c5b95-859e-5b11-a4e5-1ab13ca0ba4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa9c5b95-859e-5b11-a4e5-1ab13ca0ba4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474707} :answer-field/id #uuid "b97d107f-11ec-588d-8c72-df0e99d81ee5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "22db406c-85ef-5a5a-ab22-d062645b4362" :question/math-academy-id "q-221718" :question/problem "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $Z,$ defined by $x∼y$ if $7\\,|\\,(x-y).$ Which of the following are in the equivalence class $[5]?$\n\nI. $12$\n\nII. $-4$\n\nIII. $-2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The equivalence class $[5]$ consists of the elements that are equivalent to $5$ under the given equivalence relation. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[5] & ={x\\in Z\\,:\\,x∼5} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,:\\,7\\,|\\,(x-5)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,:\\,x=5+7k,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,-9,-2,5,12,19,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $12$ and $-2$ are in $[5],$ while $-4$ is not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3601ac83-0800-567a-9a0d-4d5c37cef413" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to an Equivalence Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22e7b59c-00d2-51c6-999a-36e8f035e54a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474876} {:answer/id #uuid "94a4b4c3-a5b5-5d59-ad59-8d61401ea0b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94a4b4c3-a5b5-5d59-ad59-8d61401ea0b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474877} :answer-field/id #uuid "70f8c5f4-4f28-5713-8c2f-b32fefee3022" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8473e63-f753-510c-841b-43db480a2ad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474878} {:answer/id #uuid "9025d27a-d49b-5c0c-831b-a614cc709a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9025d27a-d49b-5c0c-831b-a614cc709a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474879} :answer-field/id #uuid "28b2d44d-f203-5749-82f5-bc803372d4dd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475365} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99e1ee65-d53d-564c-96a8-5b357c01cffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474880} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e10a10-f5fc-50ab-9126-b670a87b72a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99e1ee65-d53d-564c-96a8-5b357c01cffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474880} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc455a4d-9c7b-57b3-8acf-8fc653209746" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c1db003-08b1-562e-8980-51389652bb7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-77205" :question/problem "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $C,$ defined by $x∼y$ if ${x}^{2}={y}^{2}.$ Which of the following are in the equivalence class $[-4]?$\n\nI. $-4$\n\nII. $4$\n\nIII. $4\\text{i}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The equivalence class $[-4]$ consists of the elements that are equivalent to $-4$ under the given equivalence relation. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-4] & ={x\\in C\\,|\\,x∼-4} \\\\  & ={x\\in C\\,|\\,{x}^{2}=(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & ={x\\in C\\,|\\,{x}^{2}=16} \\\\  & ={-4,4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-4$ and $4$ are in $[-4],$ while $4\\text{i}$ is not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421719 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152257 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dacfbca6-6135-5d51-a07e-627fce79dfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Classes Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62a4bb57-5969-52de-b010-ca21fe9a6007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474714} {:answer/id #uuid "c172fb65-6319-5c94-8438-618f08c71003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62a4bb57-5969-52de-b010-ca21fe9a6007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474714} :answer-field/id #uuid "48c6e22c-1de1-5dae-b9d0-54dcf023b85d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1dbd89d-4f75-5e11-ae6a-1bc1e6fdafbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474716} {:answer/id #uuid "a41ed67c-b2ca-5b04-b944-70698eb1053c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a41ed67c-b2ca-5b04-b944-70698eb1053c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474717} :answer-field/id #uuid "d718270d-232d-5945-ba4d-adf3b623e262" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475284} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26f18044-35d9-5b52-afe3-1a1c0f99fdcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474718} {:answer/id #uuid "e7988608-d68e-5f59-bddd-b768195a59fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26f18044-35d9-5b52-afe3-1a1c0f99fdcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474718} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6533f41-d016-573d-aa27-6228e0a41929" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46852a07-1e77-54f8-9037-1f17a12c391f" :question/math-academy-id "q-221767" :question/problem "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $R,$ defined by $x∼y$ if $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi y.$ Which of the following equivalence classes contain the element $3$\n\nI. $[0]$\n\nII. $[1]$\n\nIII. $[2]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We have $3\\in [x]$ if $3∼x.$ Using the definition of the given equivalence relation, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\cdot 3 & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\pi  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x \\\\ -1 & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $3\\notin [0]$ because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 0)=1\\ne -1\\,\\times $\n\n- $3\\in [1]$ because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)=-1\\,✓$\n\n- $3\\notin [2]$ because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 2)=1\\ne -1\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152257 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dacfbca6-6135-5d51-a07e-627fce79dfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Classes Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27afc98a-a963-5726-801e-f24814932ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474708} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9b592b-a126-5e98-882f-fa6560baf569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd9b592b-a126-5e98-882f-fa6560baf569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474709} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d217d7f-285a-533a-b5ba-bb0556c98fb1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475280} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9064f9c1-0e96-5e2c-827d-3231f222b2d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474710} {:answer/id #uuid "87364565-7c6c-5b72-9e1d-63da90081b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87364565-7c6c-5b72-9e1d-63da90081b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474711} :answer-field/id #uuid "47939426-e672-5cd9-87c9-b7d8743415ff" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475281} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1d77540-8644-5673-875e-df64580204b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474712} {:answer/id #uuid "b709fb08-f0d9-5512-a8f3-dbe810067753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1d77540-8644-5673-875e-df64580204b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474712} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c50775b-6998-5eba-a47c-4b4751871fd8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d844129-f571-5c80-934e-cfc1faad53cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-221722" :question/problem "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $Z,$ defined by $x∼y$ if $11\\,|\\,(x-y).$ Which of the following equivalence classes contain the element $-6?$\n\nI. $[5]$\n\nII. $[-17]$\n\nIII. $[-8]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We have $-6\\in [x]$ if $-6∼x.$ Using the definition of the given equivalence relation, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11\\,|\\,(-6-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $-6\\in [5]$ because $11\\,|\\,(-6-5)\\,✓$\n\n- $-6\\in [-17]$ because $11\\,|\\,(-6+17)\\,✓$\n\n- $-6\\notin [-8]$ because $11∤(-6+8)\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3601ac83-0800-567a-9a0d-4d5c37cef413" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to an Equivalence Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3632d098-f94e-51af-ba8c-9b4b134a9ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218